 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Bounded peer review — 2026-10-24 / `review-b8b2624384781d95`
+
+Production v2.0.0 is unchanged, SHA-256
+`2fe3bf8a15ae1ca7cb441755ab5b50d0acc16f12b1e23584ccd2a8d2dc2f2cfb`.
+The prior perimeter-distribution finding remains unresolved; this review did
+not repeat its census or battery.
+
+One current-source teaching counterexample is retained in the return at
+`checks/4c1d80c25a99/wall-class.json`. At seed 15, medium difficulty, consecutive
+demonstration indices 0, 1, and 2 all use color-1 walls. Replacing the authority's
+wall predicate `{1,7,9}` with literal `1` matches all three executed demo labels.
+The generated query at index 3 uses color-7 walls and disagrees in 195 cells.
+Both complete programs ran through protected Racket on all four inputs (eight
+executions); the generator's self-check accepts every retained input.
+
+This is an omitted wall-class teaching gap, not a wrong-label finding. The
+constructed lesson uses consecutive generator indices; no public-sampler census
+or universal ambiguity rate is claimed. If unseen wall classes are intentionally
+part of a transfer curriculum, label that policy explicitly. For ordinary
+supervision, teach each queried wall class or restrict queries to demonstrated
+classes. No production change is proposed as verified here.
+
+`workspace/review_wall_class.py` is a small reproducible probe, bounded to the
+first witness in seeds 0..127 and refusing an existing output file. From the
+outer packet directory, after setup:
+
+```sh
+python3 review.py run python3 generators/4c1d80c25a99/workspace/review_wall_class.py \
+  --out ../checks/4c1d80c25a99/wall-class-replay.json
+```
+
+No parametric work, full battery, acceptance, or training admission was performed.
